      "message": "An mlx5 SF has its own netdev, verbs device, and uverbs node even though its auxiliary-device path is below the parent PF BDF. On the tested BF3, enp3s0f0s0 maps to mlx5_1/uverbs1, whereas selecting by the parent BDF can open the sibling PF/uverbs0. Creating the interface from that PF would therefore create queues and flow steering for the wrong netdev. PS4 documents this use case in the commit message; the SF create/up/delete DV smoke test verified that VPP opens uverbs1.",
